      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1887 a fraudulent silver mine venture near the railroad station briefly made Garland news, with an entrepreneur selling stock and absconding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/garland_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first permanent settler, Robert Andrews, built a sawmill near Little Brokenstraw Creek around 1795, laying the groundwork for Garland’s lumber industry.",
